U.S. Chamber & Foreign Funding Resources:

I.                    The original exclusive ThinkProgress post<http://thin=
kprogress.org/2010/10/05/foreign-chamber-commerce/> on the Chamber's foreig=
n funding.
II.                  The latest ThinkProgress post: Inconvenient Facts That=
 The Chamber Hasn't Refuted<http://thinkprogress.org/2010/10/06/chamber-res=
ponse-funding/>.
III.               Today's Progress Report<http://pr.thinkprogress.org/2010=
/10/pr20101006/index.html>, "The Chamber's Foreign Influence," detailing th=
e situation and the facts.
IV.               U.S. Chamber Watch's site at www.fixtheuschamber.org<http=
://www.fixtheuschamber.org>.  Contact Samantha Brown at bsamantha@gmail.com=
<mailto:bsamantha@gmail.com> for more information on the Chamber's activiti=
es, including a full list of attack ads the Chamber has run and is running =
and the Chamber's endorsements.
V.                  A press call tomorrow at 1:30 p.m. with ThinkProgress' =
Faiz Shakir and Lee Fang and Senator Al Franken, who has publicly called fo=
r an investigation of the Chamber's foreign funding.

Call info: ( 877 ) 210 - 8943    Conference ID: 16738967
VI.               The Facts on the Chamber's Foreign Funding (see below).

WHAT WE KNOW...


 *   CHAMBER AGRESSIVELY FUNDRAISING OVERSEAS FOR GENERAL FUNDS.  The Chamb=
er has received hundreds of thousands of dollars-if not millions-in foreign=
 donations<http://thinkprogress.org/2010/10/05/foreign-chamber-commerce/> f=
rom countries like Bahrain, Abu Dhabi (U.A.E.), India, Russia, China, and e=
lsewhere following an aggressive public fundraising campaign.  ThinkProgres=
s has identified several foreign entities created by, run by, or affiliated=
 with the Chamber that return hundreds of thousands of dollars annually to =
the Chamber's general fund.  Some of these corporations are even state-owne=
d entities controlled by foreign governments.  To recap, we know of at leas=
t three ways the Chamber takes in foreign money:

       *   Direct contributions from the foreign firms, such as BP or Sieme=
ns, that are among its 300,000 members.
       *   Direct contributions from foreign firms under the auspices of "B=
usiness Councils" located in various foreign countries.  Our investigation =
has discovered that the U.S.-Bahrain Business Council and U.S.-India Busine=
ss Council have raised at least $300,000 in such direct contributions to th=
e Chamber.
       *   Indirect contributions from foreign firms who belong to their lo=
cal "AmCham," which itself in turn pays dues to the U.S. Chamber's general =
account.

 *   CHAMBER RUNNING $75 MILLION ATTACK CAMPAIGN AGAINST DEMS USING GENERAL=
 FUNDS. As of September 15, the Chamber has spent more than $6.7 million to=
 run more than 8,000 ads<http://thinkprogress.org/2010/10/05/foreign-chambe=
r-commerce/> on behalf of GOP Senate candidates alone. A new round of highl=
y misleading ads began targeting House members this week.  The Chamber says=
 it will spend some $75 million<http://www.nytimes.com/2010/10/02/us/politi=
cs/02murdoch.html?ref=3Dpolitics> on this year's election-paid for out of t=
he same general fund that the foreign money is going into.
 *   CHAMBER DISCUSSING IMPORTANCE OF 2010 ELECTION TO FOREIGN ENTITIES. To=
 galvanize foreign businesses<http://thinkprogress.org/2010/10/05/foreign-c=
hamber-commerce/>, the Chamber has commissioned former Ambassador Frank Lav=
in - who served as the McCain-Palin Asia campaign director and has appeared=
 on television multiple times recently saying a Democratic Congress is bad =
for business - to speak before various foreign Chamber affiliates to talk a=
bout the stakes for the 2010 midterm elections.
 *   WE'VE SEEN THIS MOVIE BEFORE.  The Chamber was exposed for having secr=
etly taken approximately $20 million from the health insurance industry<htt=
p://undertheinfluence.nationaljournal.com/2010/01/health-insurers-funded-ch=
amber.php>, which it then used to launch anti-health reform ads against Dem=
ocrats.  More recently, the Chamber, which receives money from BP, called o=
n taxpayers to help foot the bill<http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2010/06/10/=
chamber-of-commerce-says_n_607748.html> for BP's oil disaster in the Gulf. =
 Another secret $1 million in funding<http://www.politico.com/news/stories/=
0910/42989.html> from Fox News' parent corporation was also recently uncove=
red.

WHAT THE CHAMBER SAYS...


 *   ADMITS TO TAKING FOREIGN FUNDS. "The Chamber is proud to have global c=
ompanies<http://www.politico.com/blogs/bensmith/1010/Chamber_We_have_a_syst=
em.html?showall> among our membership."
 *   TRUST, DON'T VERIFY. The Chamber denies the allegations and claims the=
y have "a system"<http://www.politico.com/blogs/bensmith/1010/Chamber_We_ha=
ve_a_system.html?showall> in place.  As the New York Times notes today<http=
://www.nytimes.com/2010/10/06/opinion/06wed1.html?hp>: "Money, however, is =
fungible, and it is impossible for an outsider to know whether the group is=
 following its rules."

    *   When pressed further<http://voices.washingtonpost.com/plum-line/201=
0/10/us_chamber_broadens_attack_on.html> to explain whether foreign funds a=
re going into the same fund used for the political attack ads, the Chamber =
didn't deny that that was the case and once again refused to answer basic q=
uestions: "We don't feel obligated to answer that question because we follo=
w all applicable law, and no foreign money funds our voter education activi=
ties."

WHAT THE LAW SAYS...

 *   ILLEGAL FOR FOREIGN ENTITIES AND INDIVIDUALS TO SPEND IN AMERICAN ELEC=
TIONS. Under the Federal Election Campaign Act<http://www.fec.gov/pages/bro=
chures/foreign.shtml> (FECA), it is illegal for "foreign nationals" to "dir=
ectly or indirectly" contribute, donate, or spend funds in connection with =
any federal, state, or local election in the U.S.
 *   ILLEGAL FOR AMERICAN ENTITIES-LIKE THE CHAMBER-TO SOLICIT FOREIGN FUND=
S FOR AMERICAN ELECTIONS. As MoveOn's letter to the Department of Justice n=
oted: "It is not only unlawful for a foreign national to make such a contri=
bution, directly or indirectly, it is also unlawful for anyone "to solicit,=
 accept or receive" such a contribution "from a foreign national." 2 U.S.C.=
 =A7441e(a)(2)."

CALLS FOR INVESTIGATION...


 *   MOVEON.  MoveOn sent a letter to the Department of Justice Tuesday<htt=
p://www.huffingtonpost.com/2010/10/05/moveon-asks-doj-to-launch_n_751534.ht=
ml> requesting that it began an immediate investigation of the Chamber's po=
tentially illegal activities.  MoveOn has also launched a petition calling =
for the investigation and its members are calling on local TV stations to i=
mmediately take down the Chamber's ads.
 *   SENATOR FRANKEN. Senator Al Franken wrote to the Federal Election Comm=
ission<http://www.startribune.com/politics/blogs/104373294.html?elr=3DKArks=
LckD8EQDUoaEyqyP4O:DW3ckUiD3aPc:_Yyc:aUgOy9cP3DieyckcUsI> Tuesday and reque=
sted that they too began an immediate investigation, as well close certain =
loopholes that could allow foreign spending in American elections.

PERRIELLO GETS AHEAD OF POTENTIAL FOREIGN MONEY IN HIS DISTRICT...


 *   Rep. Tom Perriello held a conference call with reporters Tuesday night=
 to denounce foreign money in American elections:
    *   "This latest move is beyond outrageous, to being fundamentally un-A=
merican and undemocratic." [Lynchburg News & Advance, 10/5<http://www2.news=
advance.com/news/2010/oct/05/perriello-foreign-money-financing-attack-ads-a=
r-544575/>]
    *   "On Tuesday, Perriello called on his opponent Sen. Robert Hurt to s=
tand-up against what he calls an 'organization with shadow funding'." [WDJB=
-TV, 10/5<http://www.wdbj7.com/news/wdbj7-story-perriello-ad-100510,0,75296=
97.story>]

SECRET MONEY THREATENS TO DROWN OUT REAL PEOPLE'S VOICES...

 *   Secret money from corporate special interests - foreign and domestic -=
 threatens to drown out the voices and concerns of everyday Americans.  Rig=
ht-wing third-party groups are preparing to spend a whopping $400 MILLION<h=
ttp://thinkprogress.org/2010/08/27/conservative-groups-400-millio/>, much o=
f it from secret sources, to buy our election.  The American people - not s=
pecial interests - should decide our elections.


Josh Dorner
Communications Director, Progressive Media
tel 202.481.8153
cel 202.679.7570

